{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:4048e8b143f096e0","name":"Pelagia Duplex Command Assault Gunship","source":{"id":"source:reference-4048e8b143f096e0","title":"Pelagia Duplex Command Assault Gunship","revision":19283,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:39:40Z","sha256":"7a74a4b989274978c872e86ae392fd48c3ea6b6d14dfd7974eb32e6d75e10b20","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19283","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Pelagia%20Duplex%20Command%20Assault%20Gunship&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-4048e8b143f096e0","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Designed by House Pelagia engineers in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Tapani Sector"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Tapani_Sector?action=edit&redlink=1"},", the Pelagia Duplex Command Assault Gunship- dubbed the \"Orphanmaker\" by its designers- defends Tapani Space from the onslaught of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}," during ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Great Sith War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Great_Sith_War"},". Boasting two cockpits and two gunnery pods, the Orphanmaker is a military vessel outfitted for use in the private fleets of the Lords of the Expanse. With the threat of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Great Sith War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Great_Sith_War"}," gone (for a time), House Pelagia has no qualms in selling these well-equipped gunships to outside buyers, and they significantly increase their family holdings with profits reaped from the Orphanmaker design.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The 30-meter-long Command Assault Gunship requires five crew members to operate at optimal functionality, though it can be flown effectively with only a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," and one other crew member. The Duplex Command Assault Gunship also features numerous built-in weapon mounts and power supply conduits, making it easier to install new ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Systems"}," and upgrading existing weapons than any other ship of its size (granting a +5 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"}," bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," checks made to install ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Systems"},"). A number of these ships are sold off just prior to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Mandalorian Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Mandalorian_Wars"}," and bought by wealthy individuals and bounty hunters, including ",{"tag":"a","children":["Del Moomo"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Del_Moomo","referenceId":"reference:9c3278be49e9b560"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dob Moomo"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dob_Moomo","referenceId":"reference:d99179aa60020d3f"}," (whose heavily armed custom Orphanmaker is called ",{"tag":"a","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Moomo Williwaw"]}],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Moomo_Williwaw","referenceId":"reference:bbbd643564831f5c"},").\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Expert)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Pelagia Duplex Command Assault Gunship Statistics (CL 12)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transport"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transport"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","childr